-- ============================================================================
-- 0013 — the 13 Maa Baglamukhi sub-services
-- ============================================================================
-- The category "Maa Baglamukhi Puja & Havan" held exactly one service ("Maa
-- Baglamukhi Havan"), while the business sells thirteen distinct intents
-- underneath it — court case, shatru stambhan, business growth, santan prapti
-- and so on. This inserts those thirteen as services in that category, which
-- is the only sub-service level the schema has: category -> service. There is
-- no services.parent_id, and adding one would mean a new nesting level in the
-- public routes, the admin editor, the SEO render layer and the AI mappings —
-- far more than "list the sub-services" actually needs.
--
-- Content comes from the research-based sub-service master authored for this
-- catalogue. Two deliberate departures from that document:
--
--   1. Its overviews and several FAQ answers are written to the site owner
--      ("PanditSuggest should explain this as...", "Do not promise..."). Those
--      are editorial instructions, not devotee-facing copy, and the one
--      service already in this category shows what happens when they are
--      pasted through: its live description ends mid-sentence in "On
--      PanditSuggest, benefits should be pres...". They are rewritten here as
--      prose addressed to the devotee, keeping every no-guarantee commitment
--      intact — no promise of a court win, an election, profit, a cure, a
--      marriage, a conception, or the removal of black magic.
--   2. process[].duration is left blank rather than filled with invented
--      per-step timings. The source gives none, and a fabricated "15 min" on a
--      ritual step is exactly the kind of detail a devotee would rely on.
--
-- INSERTED INACTIVE (is_active = FALSE) on purpose. These have no images yet;
-- an admin uploads one per service, checks the copy, and flips each live from
-- the admin panel. Nothing appears on the public site until then.
--
-- Every field written here is one the admin services editor round-trips
-- (repositories/admin/services.repository.js): the JSONB shapes are exactly
-- benefits [{icon,title,detail}], process [{step,title,detail,duration}],
-- samagri_list [{item,qty}] and faqs [{q,a}], so opening one of these in the
-- admin panel and pressing Save cannot silently reshape it.
--
-- content_hi is deliberately NOT written. It is the translator's output
-- (services/hindiContent.service.js), produced on an admin save; a Hindi
-- reader falls back to English per field until then, which is the same
-- behaviour as any newly created service.
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING. Re-running never overwrites an
-- admin's later edits.
-- ============================================================================

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The parent category must exist. Resolved by slug with a fallback to the
-- exact name: the live slug is 'maa-baglamukhi-puja & havan' — a space and an
-- ampersand, produced by whatever created it — and a future tidy-up of that
-- slug should not turn this migration into a NOT NULL violation on
-- services.category_id with no explanation.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DO $guard$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.service_categories
     WHERE slug = 'maa-baglamukhi-puja & havan'
        OR name = 'Maa Baglamukhi Puja & Havan'
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Migration 0013: the "Maa Baglamukhi Puja & Havan" service category does not exist — create it before loading its sub-services';
  END IF;
END
$guard$;

WITH cat AS (
  SELECT id FROM public.service_categories
   WHERE slug = 'maa-baglamukhi-puja & havan'
      OR name = 'Maa Baglamukhi Puja & Havan'
   ORDER BY (slug = 'maa-baglamukhi-puja & havan') DESC
   LIMIT 1
),
incoming (name, slug, icon_name, display_order,
          description, short_description, estimated_duration,
          recommended_muhurat, online_note,
          benefits, process, samagri_list, faqs) AS (
  VALUES
  ('Court Case Vijay Puja', 'court-case-vijay-baglamukhi-puja', 'book-open', 10,
   'Court Case Vijay Puja is a purpose-based Maa Baglamukhi ritual. You give a clear legal sankalp — an ongoing court matter, a property dispute, a service matter, family litigation or a false accusation — and the pandit performs Maa Baglamukhi pujan, mantra-japa and havan in your name and gotra. Baglamukhi worship is traditionally associated with stambhan, the stilling of harmful speech, hostile intent and opposition, which is why Nalkheda practitioners have long offered it to devotees under legal pressure. It is offered here as a devotional prayer for protection, confidence and a just outcome — never as a guarantee of winning a case, and never as a replacement for your advocate. Choose this service if you are dealing with an ongoing court case, a property or inheritance dispute, a false allegation, service or employment litigation, a family or matrimonial legal matter, or repeated hearing-related stress.',
   'For devotees facing a court case, property dispute, legal notice, false allegation or prolonged litigation. Performed as a prayer for courage, clarity, protection from hostile speech and a fair resolution.',
   '2-4 hours (standard); longer with mantra-anushthan',
   'Chosen with the officiating pandit based on case urgency, your sankalp and the local Panchang. Tuesday, Thursday/Friday and auspicious Devi tithis are commonly used by practitioners, but there is no single compulsory time.',
   'Live sankalp participation is available. Booked as a Nalkheda service, the physical havan is performed by the pandit at Nalkheda while you join remotely.',
   '[{"icon":"🛡️","title":"Legal-pressure support","detail":"Traditionally sought for inner steadiness and spiritual protection through the length of a case."},{"icon":"🗣️","title":"Speech protection prayer","detail":"Baglamukhi worship is associated with the restraint of harmful or hostile speech."},{"icon":"🔥","title":"Courage and clarity","detail":"The sankalp and mantra process support focus before hearings, meetings and decisions."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Obstacle pacification","detail":"Devotees pray for a reduction in repeated procedural or opposition-related obstacles."},{"icon":"⚖️","title":"Fair-resolution prayer","detail":"The ritual is offered with the intention of justice and an appropriate resolution."},{"icon":"🧘","title":"Mental peace","detail":"A structured devotional practice to hold on to through a stressful legal phase."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Case Sankalp & Naam-Gotra","detail":"The pandit records your name, gotra if known, the type of case and the exact prayer intention.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Shuddhi, Ganesh & Guru Pujan","detail":"Purification and opening prayers are performed before the main Baglamukhi ritual.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Maa Baglamukhi Avahan & Pujan","detail":"The Devi is invoked with yellow flowers, turmeric, akshat, dhupa, deepa and naivedya.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Baglamukhi Mantra Jaap","detail":"A declared mantra count is recited for the legal sankalp.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Court Case Havan","detail":"Ahutis are offered into the sacred fire with Baglamukhi mantra and the prescribed samagri.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti, Aarti & Sankalp Samarpan","detail":"The ritual closes with the final offering, a prayer for justice, aarti and prasad.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"item":"Yellow cloth","qty":"1"},{"item":"Maa Baglamukhi image/yantra","qty":"1"},{"item":"Kalash, coconut, mango leaves","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Turmeric / haldi pieces","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Yellow flowers / marigold","qty":"1-2 garlands + loose flowers"},{"item":"Yellow akshat / rice","qty":"1 bowl"},{"item":"Ghee","qty":"250-500 ml for standard havan"},{"item":"Havan samagri","qty":"1 standard pack"},{"item":"Mango wood / samidha","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Roli, moli, sandal, supari","qty":"1 puja set"},{"item":"Incense, camphor, cotton wicks","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Case papers/photo","qty":"optional, kept respectfully near the sankalp; never placed in the fire"}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"q":"Does this puja guarantee that I will win my court case?","a":"No. It is a spiritual and devotional ritual. Court outcomes depend on facts, law, evidence and the judicial process."},{"q":"What details are required?","a":"Your name, gotra if known, city, the nature of the case and a simple sankalp. The case number is optional unless the pandit specifically asks for it."},{"q":"Can it be performed without me travelling to Nalkheda?","a":"Yes. The pandit can take your sankalp remotely and you may join through live video where that option is available."},{"q":"Is Lal Mirch Havan compulsory for court cases?","a":"No. Some practitioners use special havan variations, but the exact samagri should be selected by the acharya rather than assumed."},{"q":"How long does it take?","a":"A standard puja-havan is usually around 2-4 hours. A larger mantra-anushthan can take longer."},{"q":"Can I submit my legal papers for the puja?","a":"A copy can be respectfully kept near the sankalp if the priest permits. Original legal documents should never be risked or burned."},{"q":"Should I stop legal consultation after the puja?","a":"No. Continue with a qualified advocate and keep every legal deadline. The puja is complementary spiritual support."}]'::jsonb),

  ('Shatru Stambhan Puja', 'shatru-stambhan-baglamukhi-puja', 'shield-check', 20,
   'Shatru Stambhan is one of the best-known intent-based forms of Baglamukhi worship. Stambhan means to still, restrain or immobilise. In plain terms, this service is for someone who feels continuously disturbed by hostile opposition, malicious speech, intimidation, rivalry or deliberate obstruction. The ritual uses a personalised sankalp, Maa Baglamukhi pujan, mantra-japa and havan. It is performed as protection and pacification: the prayer is that harmful conduct, speech and interference lose their power over you. It is never performed to physically harm, curse or destroy anyone. Choose this service if you face persistent hostile opposition, malicious speech or defamation-like pressure, workplace or business rivalry, repeated interference, fear caused by adversaries, or simply need protection and confidence.',
   'For devotees facing persistent opposition, harmful speech, harassment-like pressure or repeated interference. A prayer to restrain hostile intent and protect the devotee — not to harm another person.',
   '2-4 hours',
   'Pandit-guided. Tuesday, Friday, Ashtami and Baglamukhi-related auspicious periods are commonly preferred, but the exact timing varies by tradition.',
   'Live sankalp participation is possible — the pandit takes your sankalp remotely and you may join the ritual by video.',
   '[{"icon":"🛡️","title":"Opposition pacification","detail":"Traditionally sought to reduce the effect of hostile intent and obstruction."},{"icon":"🗣️","title":"Protection from harmful speech","detail":"Baglamukhi is especially associated with control of destructive speech."},{"icon":"🔥","title":"Inner courage","detail":"Supports steadiness while dealing with confrontation or rivalry."},{"icon":"🧘","title":"Mental composure","detail":"Encourages a calm response instead of reactive behaviour."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Boundary and protection sankalp","detail":"The ritual focuses on spiritual distance from harmful influence."},{"icon":"🕉️","title":"Devi upasana","detail":"Focused worship of Maa Baglamukhi for strength and protection."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Concern & Sankalp","detail":"You explain the nature of the opposition, without asking for harm to any person.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Shuddhi & Ganesh Pujan","detail":"Opening purification, Ganesh worship and guru remembrance.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Baglamukhi Avahan","detail":"Maa Baglamukhi is invoked with the yellow upacharas.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Stambhan-oriented Mantra Jaap","detail":"The acharya performs the selected mantra-japa for protection and restraint of hostility.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Shatru Stambhan Havan","detail":"Havan is performed with the prescribed Baglamukhi samagri and mantra ahutis.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti & Shanti Prarthana","detail":"The final prayer is directed toward protection, peace and an end to harmful interference.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"item":"Yellow cloth","qty":"1"},{"item":"Baglamukhi image/yantra","qty":"1"},{"item":"Haldi / turmeric pieces","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Yellow mustard / chana dal","qty":"as advised by the pandit"},{"item":"Yellow flowers","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Kalash & coconut","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Ghee","qty":"250-500 ml"},{"item":"Havan samagri","qty":"1 pack"},{"item":"Samidha / havan wood","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Akshat, roli, moli, sandal","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Incense, camphor, lamp","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Naivedya / fruit or yellow sweets","qty":"as required"}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"q":"What does “Stambhan” mean here?","a":"It means the spiritual restraint or stilling of harmful opposition, speech or interference."},{"q":"Is this puja intended to hurt an enemy?","a":"No. It is never performed for physical harm, coercion or revenge — only for protection, peace and the restraint of harmful conduct."},{"q":"Do I need to give the other person''s name?","a":"Some priests may ask for context, but the service can be performed with your own protection sankalp. Avoid sharing unnecessary personal details."},{"q":"Can it be done for workplace rivalry?","a":"Yes. Devotees commonly seek it for professional or business opposition, as a prayer for protection and obstacle pacification."},{"q":"Can I join online?","a":"Yes, where the performing pandit offers live sankalp."},{"q":"How is it different from Shatru Nash Puja?","a":"Stambhan focuses on restraining harmful opposition. Shatru Nash is offered as the removal of the problem''s influence — in both cases, never the destruction of a person."},{"q":"Are results guaranteed?","a":"No. It is a traditional spiritual practice, not a guaranteed practical outcome."}]'::jsonb),

  ('Shatru Nash & Protection Puja', 'shatru-nash-protection-baglamukhi-puja', 'trishul', 30,
   'Nalkheda practitioners commonly use the name Shatru Nashak or Shatru Nash Puja, and the meaning deserves to be stated plainly: the prayer is that the harmful influence — the fear, the harassment, the rivalry, the obstruction — comes to an end. The ritual follows Maa Baglamukhi pujan, mantra-japa, havan and purnahuti. Some lineages use special havan samagri or a longer anushthan depending on the situation, which the assigned pandit will tell you in advance. This service is never offered as a way to destroy an enemy; it is a protection and obstacle-removal sankalp. Choose it if you face severe opposition pressure, fear from adversaries, repeated harassment-like interference, a long-running rivalry, or need protection and peace during and after sustained hostility.',
   'A stronger protection-oriented Baglamukhi puja for devotees severely troubled by opposition, fear or persistent hostile interference. Here “Shatru Nash” means the removal of the harmful influence — never harm to a person.',
   '2-4 hours',
   'Selected by the pandit based on your sankalp and the Panchang. Devi tithis and Tuesday/Friday are commonly used by practitioners.',
   'Live sankalp participation is possible. The pandit performs the physical havan and you join remotely or by sankalp.',
   '[{"icon":"🕊️","title":"Removal of harmful influence","detail":"The prayer is that hostile interference no longer controls your life."},{"icon":"🛡️","title":"Protection","detail":"Traditionally sought for spiritual safeguarding during conflict."},{"icon":"🔥","title":"Fear reduction","detail":"Supports courage and emotional steadiness."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Obstacle removal","detail":"Focused on ending the repeated blocks created by conflict or rivalry."},{"icon":"🤝","title":"Conflict de-escalation prayer","detail":"The closing sankalp seeks peace and a just end to hostility."},{"icon":"🕉️","title":"Spiritual discipline","detail":"Mantra and havan create a focused devotional practice."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Protection Sankalp","detail":"The purpose is recorded in non-harmful terms: safety, peace and an end to interference.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Purification & Ganesh Pujan","detail":"The standard opening shuddhi and Ganesh worship.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Maa Baglamukhi Pujan","detail":"Yellow offerings and the Devi upacharas are offered.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Mantra Jaap","detail":"The selected Baglamukhi mantra is recited for protection and obstacle removal.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Shatru Nashak / Protection Havan","detail":"Havan ahutis are made as prescribed by the acharya.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti & Shanti Sankalp","detail":"The ritual closes with a prayer for safety, justice and a peaceful resolution.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"item":"Yellow cloth","qty":"1"},{"item":"Baglamukhi image/yantra","qty":"1"},{"item":"Haldi","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Yellow flowers","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Kalash & coconut","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Ghee","qty":"250-500 ml"},{"item":"Havan samagri","qty":"1 pack"},{"item":"Yellow mustard / gram","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Akshat / rice","qty":"1 bowl"},{"item":"Incense, camphor, wicks","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Puja thali basics","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Naivedya","qty":"as required"}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"q":"Why is it called Shatru Nash?","a":"Traditionally the term refers to ending enemy-related trouble. Here it means the removal of a harmful influence, not the destruction of a person."},{"q":"Is it stronger than Shatru Stambhan?","a":"Practitioners often position it as a stronger or more intensive intent, but the actual ritual depth depends on the acharya and the package you choose."},{"q":"Can it be done if I do not know who is opposing me?","a":"Yes. A general protection and obstacle-removal sankalp can be used."},{"q":"Does it involve black magic?","a":"No. Authentic Baglamukhi worship is performed here as a devotional protective ritual; harmful occult practices are not offered."},{"q":"Can I participate online?","a":"Yes, where live sankalp is offered."},{"q":"How long does it take?","a":"Usually 2-4 hours for a standard puja-havan. An extended anushthan may run over several days."},{"q":"Will it solve a police or legal issue automatically?","a":"No. Please use the appropriate legal and safety channels alongside any spiritual practice."}]'::jsonb),

  ('Political / Rajneeti Vijay Puja', 'rajneeti-vijay-baglamukhi-puja', 'award', 40,
   'Rajneeti Vijay, or Political Success Puja, is a purpose-based Baglamukhi service offered by several Nalkheda practitioners. The sankalp may relate to an election, a leadership responsibility, public criticism, political opposition or an important campaign. The spiritual logic is Baglamukhi''s traditional association with speech, confidence, opposition and stambhan. It is performed as a prayer for clear speech, courage, protection from unfair hostility and success in legitimate public work — never for the manipulation of voters, the coercion of opponents, or a guaranteed election victory. Choose this service if you are running an election campaign, carrying public leadership responsibility, facing political opposition or reputation pressure, preparing an important public speech, or working through a difficult leadership decision.',
   'For candidates, public representatives and people in leadership seeking spiritual strength during elections, public opposition, reputation pressure or difficult political work.',
   '2-4 hours',
   'Pandit-guided. Some Nalkheda practitioners prefer Tuesday, Friday, Baglamukhi Jayanti or a chart-based auspicious muhurat.',
   'Live sankalp participation is possible, so a campaign schedule need not be interrupted to attend in person.',
   '[{"icon":"🔥","title":"Confidence in public life","detail":"Devotees seek courage and steadiness through political pressure."},{"icon":"🗣️","title":"Speech discipline","detail":"Baglamukhi worship is traditionally linked with control of speech and debate."},{"icon":"🛡️","title":"Protection from hostility","detail":"A prayer for protection from unfair opposition and malicious attacks."},{"icon":"🏅","title":"Karya siddhi sankalp","detail":"Performed for the successful completion of legitimate political work."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Reputation steadiness","detail":"A devotional prayer for dignity and composure in public life."},{"icon":"🧘","title":"Leadership clarity","detail":"Supports a calm and focused mindset before important decisions."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Political / Leadership Sankalp","detail":"The exact legitimate objective is stated: an election, leadership work, a speech or public service.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Ganesh & Guru Pujan","detail":"Opening prayers and purification.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Baglamukhi Avahan","detail":"Devi worship with the yellow offerings.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Vijaya / Vak Shakti Mantra Jaap","detail":"Mantra-japa for confidence, speech discipline and protection.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Rajneeti Vijay Havan","detail":"Havan ahutis are offered for karya siddhi and protection.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti & Aarti","detail":"A closing prayer for ethical success, public welfare and peace.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"item":"Yellow cloth","qty":"1"},{"item":"Baglamukhi image/yantra","qty":"1"},{"item":"Yellow flowers","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Turmeric","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Kalash & coconut","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Ghee","qty":"250-500 ml"},{"item":"Havan samagri","qty":"1 pack"},{"item":"Akshat / rice","qty":"1 bowl"},{"item":"Yellow sweets / fruits","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Incense, camphor, lamp","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Puja thali basics","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Campaign symbol/photo","qty":"optional, and only for a respectful sankalp — not for burning"}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"q":"Is this only for election candidates?","a":"No. It can also be booked by people in public leadership or political work who want a devotional sankalp for courage and clarity."},{"q":"Does it guarantee election victory?","a":"No. Election outcomes depend on voters, law, campaigning and many real-world factors."},{"q":"Can it be performed for a speech or an important meeting?","a":"Yes. The sankalp can focus on clear speech, confidence and protection from hostile pressure."},{"q":"Can it be done online?","a":"Yes, with live sankalp participation."},{"q":"Is a kundli required?","a":"Not always, though some practitioners use birth details to choose the muhurat."},{"q":"Is the puja ever done against an opponent?","a":"No. Control over voters, the silencing of opponents and any coercive intent are outside what is offered here."},{"q":"How long does it take?","a":"Usually 2-4 hours for the standard ritual."}]'::jsonb),

  ('Business Growth Puja', 'business-growth-baglamukhi-puja', 'sparkles', 50,
   'Business Growth Puja is widely listed by Nalkheda Baglamukhi practitioners. The ritual is performed with the business or firm name together with the owner''s naam-gotra sankalp. It combines Baglamukhi worship for protection and obstacle pacification with prosperity-oriented prayers, and depending on the pandit''s tradition, Lakshmi or Kuber worship may be included — your package will say exactly what is covered. It suits a devotee looking for spiritual support around slow growth, competitive pressure, blocked payments or a new venture. It is not a guaranteed profit, sales or investment-return service. Choose it if you face slow business growth, competitive pressure, blocked payments, a new venture or expansion, repeated operational obstacles, or the ordinary stress of running a business.',
   'For business owners facing stagnation, competitive pressure, blocked payments, repeated obstacles or uncertainty. Combines Maa Baglamukhi protection with a prosperity-oriented sankalp.',
   '2-3 hours',
   'Friday, an auspicious business-start muhurat, or another date selected by the pandit. The business name and the owner''s sankalp can both be included.',
   'Live sankalp participation is possible, with the firm name and owner details taken remotely before the ritual.',
   '[{"icon":"✨","title":"Business prosperity prayer","detail":"Traditionally sought for auspicious growth and stability."},{"icon":"🛡️","title":"Competitor-pressure protection","detail":"A prayer for protection from unfair rivalry and negative influence."},{"icon":"🧘","title":"Decision clarity","detail":"The sankalp supports calmness and focus in business decisions."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Obstacle pacification","detail":"Devotees pray for smoother progress in commercial work."},{"icon":"💰","title":"Payment-flow sankalp","detail":"A prayer around delayed receivables can be included, without financial guarantees."},{"icon":"🏺","title":"Positive business beginning","detail":"Suitable before launching, reopening or expanding a venture."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Business Sankalp","detail":"The business name, owner details and the main concern are recorded.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Ganesh & Kalash Pujan","detail":"Opening worship for auspiciousness.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Baglamukhi & Prosperity Pujan","detail":"Maa Baglamukhi is worshipped; some traditions add Lakshmi or Kuber prayers.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Mantra Jaap","detail":"Baglamukhi and prosperity mantra counts are recited as declared.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Vyapar Vriddhi Havan","detail":"Fire offerings are made with the prescribed yellow and prosperity samagri.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti & Business Prarthana","detail":"A closing prayer for ethical growth, stability and wise action.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"item":"Yellow cloth","qty":"1"},{"item":"Baglamukhi image/yantra","qty":"1"},{"item":"Lakshmi/Kuber image or Shri Yantra","qty":"optional, by tradition"},{"item":"Kalash & coconut","qty":"1 set"},{"item":"Yellow flowers / lotus if available","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Turmeric / yellow mustard","qty":"as advised"},{"item":"Rice / akshat","qty":"1 bowl"},{"item":"Ghee","qty":"250-500 ml"},{"item":"Havan samagri","qty":"1 pack"},{"item":"Coins","qty":"symbolic offering, small quantity"},{"item":"Fruits / sweets","qty":"as required"},{"item":"Business card / firm name sheet","qty":"optional, for the sankalp only"}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"q":"Can I book this for a new business?","a":"Yes. It is commonly used as an auspicious beginning and a protection-oriented business sankalp."},{"q":"Can it help with blocked payments?","a":"A blocked-payment concern can be included in the sankalp, but the puja does not guarantee the recovery of money."},{"q":"Is Lakshmi Puja included?","a":"Some Nalkheda practitioners combine Baglamukhi and Lakshmi-oriented worship. Your service package states clearly what is included."},{"q":"Do I need my company documents?","a":"No. The firm or business name and the owner''s details are usually enough for the sankalp."},{"q":"Can partners join together?","a":"Yes. All relevant owners and partners can be included if the pandit permits."},{"q":"Can it be online?","a":"Yes."},{"q":"Should practical business action continue?","a":"Yes. Spiritual worship complements accounting, sales, contracts, legal advice and business planning — it does not replace them."}]'::jsonb),

  ('Lakshmi / Dhan Prapti Puja', 'lakshmi-dhan-prapti-baglamukhi-puja', 'kalash', 60,
   'Dhan Prapti and Lakshmi Prapti services appear in Nalkheda practitioner catalogues as prosperity-oriented Baglamukhi rituals. The exact deity combination and mantra method vary by lineage: some use Maa Baglamukhi with Lakshmi, the Shri Yantra, Kuber or other prosperity mantras, and the assigned pandit will tell you which applies to your booking. It is offered as a prayer for financial stability, responsible prosperity and the removal of perceived spiritual obstacles around money. It does not promise sudden wealth, debt cancellation, lottery success or a guaranteed income. Choose it for a financial stability prayer, repeated money obstacles, business prosperity, a new financial beginning, a household prosperity sankalp, or simply as gratitude and abundance worship.',
   'A prosperity-focused devotional service for financial stability, a dhan-prapti sankalp and relief from repeated money-related obstacles, often combining Maa Baglamukhi with Lakshmi-oriented worship.',
   '2-3 hours',
   'Friday, Diwali-related auspicious periods, or a muhurat selected by the pandit.',
   'Live sankalp participation is possible; the family or business prosperity sankalp is taken in your name remotely.',
   '[{"icon":"🏺","title":"Prosperity prayer","detail":"Devotees seek auspicious financial stability and abundance."},{"icon":"🪔","title":"Money-obstacle pacification","detail":"A devotional sankalp for repeated financial blockages."},{"icon":"🌸","title":"Lakshmi blessings","detail":"Many traditions add Lakshmi-oriented worship for Shri and prosperity."},{"icon":"🙏","title":"Responsible abundance","detail":"The ritual reinforces gratitude and the disciplined use of resources."},{"icon":"🏠","title":"Business or household auspiciousness","detail":"Suitable for a family or business prosperity sankalp."},{"icon":"✨","title":"Positive new beginning","detail":"Often chosen before a venture, a purchase or a financial reset."}]'::jsonb,
   '[{"step":1,"title":"Financial Sankalp","detail":"You state a simple and ethical prosperity intention.","duration":""},{"step":2,"title":"Ganesh & Kalash Pujan","detail":"The opening worship.","duration":""},{"step":3,"title":"Baglamukhi-Lakshmi Pujan","detail":"Maa Baglamukhi and, where included, Lakshmi or the Shri Yantra are worshipped.","duration":""},{"step":4,"title":"Prosperity Mantra Jaap","detail":"The declared mantra count is recited.","duration":""},{"step":5,"title":"Dhan Prapti Havan","detail":"Havan with ghee, grains and the prescribed prosperity and yellow samagri.","duration":""},{"step":6,"title":"Purnahuti & Aarti","detail":"A final prayer for stability, gratitude and ethical prosperity.","duration":""}]'::jsonb,
